text:
Score: 5/10. The code is small, readable, and the existing tests pass, but I would not approve it as-is. The main problems are data integrity and reporting correctness: failed ingests can still mutate the DB, timestamps are stored/queried in ways that produce wrong results, and real Slurm TRES/state values are mishandled.

I estimate about 180 lines need meaningful change in production code, with a similar amount of targeted test work advisable. I did not find a major security issue; the SQL injection surface is mostly controlled by parameterization and a `group_by` allowlist.

Verification run: `python -m pytest -q` passed: 12 tests, 1 pytest cache warning from the read-only workspace.

```json
{
  "score": 5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "83-99",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Malformed-row threshold is checked after committed upserts, so a failed ingest can still persist partial data."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/store.py",
      "lines": "114,130,161,178,198-199",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Timestamp filters and max-window logic compare raw ISO strings lexicographically, producing wrong results for date-only or offset timestamps."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/parsing.py",
      "lines": "109-125",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Timestamps are validated but returned unnormalized, allowing inconsistent date-only, naive, and timezone-aware values into storage."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/parsing.py",
      "lines": "91-105",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "GPU TRES parsing matches any key starting with gres/gpu, so gres/gpumem and gres/gpuutil are treated as GPU counts or hard failures."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/store.py",
      "lines": "11",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Failure-state detection omits Slurm OUT_OF_MEMORY, so documented out-of-memory failures are excluded from failure reports."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/parsing.py",
      "lines": "132-135",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Rows with extra pipe-delimited columns are silently accepted because DictReader's None overflow field is ignored."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "77-87",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Ingest only catches RowParseError, so decode, permission, and SQLite errors can crash with a traceback instead of a CLI error."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/store.py",
      "lines": "18-22",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "All report paths create and initialize a database, so a typo in --db silently reports against a new empty DB."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/jobwatch/parsing.py",
      "lines": "175-200",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "The parser loads every valid job into memory before writing, which will scale poorly for large sacct exports."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 180,
  "approve": false
}
```
